(361727, 28529, 472, '<td valign="top">now this is original. i like it!  great execution too. cant wait to see how you did it.</td>', 'now this is original. i like it!  great execution too. cant wait to see how you did it.', '2003-07-20 22:27:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(361728, 28548, 472, '<td valign="top">interesting placement of sun and ice!  i think, though, this would have been stronger with either a) no person , or b) the person at a completely different angle  - maybe in sillhouette.</td>', 'interesting placement of sun and ice!  i think, though, this would have been stronger with either a) no person , or b) the person at a completely different angle  - maybe in sillhouette.', '2003-07-20 22:29:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(361737, 28073, 8911, '<td valign="top">Nice - I like the fact the glass is sweating in particular; it underlines the heat. The sun glare is a nice effect as well, not overwhelming.</td>', 'Nice - I like the fact the glass is sweating in particular; it underlines the heat. The sun glare is a nice effect as well, not overwhelming.', '2003-07-20 22:44:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(361740, 28603, 8911, '<td valign="top">There seems to be a lot of dead space in this photo that is just black - it''s a fascinating choice, to take it in the dark, and I''d have liked to see the flames and whatever is being sterilized fill the frame more completely.</td>', 'There seems to be a lot of dead space in this photo that is just black - it''s a fascinating choice, to take it in the dark, and I''d have liked to see the flames and whatever is being sterilized fill the frame more completely.', '2003-07-20 22:51:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(361742, 28422, 8911, '<td valign="top">You have a very patient model.... :) I like the lines, and the negative space at the top, although the shadows at right and the lower left are deep enough to drain some of the detail.</td>', 'You have a very patient model.... :) I like the lines, and the negative space at the top, although the shadows at right and the lower left are deep enough to drain some of the detail.', '2003-07-20 23:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(361743, 28724, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is an attractive photo. The glare from the candle''s flame detracts from it a bit - overwhelms that section of the photo - and I wonder if you might have been able to tone that down partly somehow. A slower exposure might well have made the lower ice cubes too dim to see as clear detail (and the amount of detail in the middle layer is really nice). Possibly partly obscuring the flame behind an ice cube would help, but it might also have made it worse - I don''t know if you tried these.<br/> <br/>At any rate, while I think that could improve it if some way could be found to do it at all, it''s still a lovely photo as-is.</td>', 'This is an attractive photo. The glare from the candle''s flame detracts from it a bit - overwhelms that section of the photo - and I wonder if you might have been able to tone that down partly somehow. A slower exposure might well have made the lower ice cubes too dim to see as clear detail (and the amount of detail in the middle layer is really nice). Possibly partly obscuring the flame behind an ice cube would help, but it might also have made it worse - I don''t know if you tried these. At any rate, while I think that could improve it if some way could be found to do it at all, it''s still a lovely photo as-is.', '2003-07-20 23:05:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(361744, 28557, 8911, '<td valign="top">Nice - a tiny bit more shadowed than I would like, but I don''t know how you could correct for that without having the flames too bright, unless you could have gotten a very dim light on the scene from above.<br/> <br/>I''m guessing the object on the left is another candle, in a candle-holder, but I''m not completely sure - it''s that detail, more than any other, that I''d like to be able to make out.<br/> <br/>The reddish colors of this photo, and the composition, are absolutely gorgeous - I like the balancing of the ''weight'' of the objects.</td>', 'Nice - a tiny bit more shadowed than I would like, but I don''t know how you could correct for that without having the flames too bright, unless you could have gotten a very dim light on the scene from above. I''m guessing the object on the left is another candle, in a candle-holder, but I''m not completely sure - it''s that detail, more than any other, that I''d like to be able to make out. The reddish colors of this photo, and the composition, are absolutely gorgeous - I like the balancing of the ''weight'' of the objects.', '2003-07-20 23:07:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(361746, 28766, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a nice picture - I wish the focus were a bit crisper (it seems to have settled on the trees that bulk in the left side of the picture, rather than the rafters), but it definitely conveys the scene. Makes me wish I were there, especially after the weather today....</td>', 'This is a nice picture - I wish the focus were a bit crisper (it seems to have settled on the trees that bulk in the left side of the picture, rather than the rafters), but it definitely conveys the scene. Makes me wish I were there, especially after the weather today....', '2003-07-20 23:16:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(361747, 28733, 8911, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. I like the balance and feel of this photo, the cool greens, the rock bulking at the right. Cool, and also serene; this looks like a place I''d like to sit and just be for a while.<br/> <br/>With ''fishing'' as your topic, though, it''s a pity the person is not in slightly better focus - I can make out the fishing pole, but the upper part of it only by staring and applying my imagination. I''d hate to trade off the crisp focus on the other parts of the picture for focus there, though - this is an image that would be really showy with crisp focus through the whole, rather than a shallower depth of focus, I think.</td>', 'Very pretty. I like the balance and feel of this photo, the cool greens, the rock bulking at the right. Cool, and also serene; this looks like a place I''d like to sit and just be for a while. With ''fishing'' as your topic, though, it''s a pity the person is not in slightly better focus - I can make out the fishing pole, but the upper part of it only by staring and applying my imagination. I''d hate to trade off the crisp focus on the other parts of the picture for focus there, though - this is an image that would be really showy with crisp focus through the whole, rather than a shallower depth of focus, I think.', '2003-07-20 23:18:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(361749, 28712, 8911, '<td valign="top">Is that a flower encased in ice and then melted? Or just set over ice? I''m a bit confused about the real-world setup of this photo - but the composition and the colors are lovely. I like the reflection, although the fact that it''s somewhat doubled is a bit dizzying; my eyes struggle to bring the reflection clear (it almost seems like it should be), yet of course, can''t, because it isn''t. I like that tension, it''s just a little disturbing at first glance.</td>', 'Is that a flower encased in ice and then melted? Or just set over ice? I''m a bit confused about the real-world setup of this photo - but the composition and the colors are lovely. I like the reflection, although the fact that it''s somewhat doubled is a bit dizzying; my eyes struggle to bring the reflection clear (it almost seems like it should be), yet of course, can''t, because it isn''t. I like that tension, it''s just a little disturbing at first glance.', '2003-07-20 23:21:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(361750, 28351, 2130, '<td valign="top">normally I don´t like photos of kids that much, but this one is adorable, congrats on a wonderful photo, surely a 10 :)</td>', 'normally I don´t like photos of kids that much, but this one is adorable, congrats on a wonderful photo, surely a 10 :)', '2003-07-20 23:21:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(361751, 28702, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but I''d like to see the thermometer from an angle that made it easier to read, given the question the title poses (even if the actual temperature was out of the shot - it would feel more complete that way, I think).</td>', 'I like the idea, but I''d like to see the thermometer from an angle that made it easier to read, given the question the title poses (even if the actual temperature was out of the shot - it would feel more complete that way, I think).', '2003-07-20 23:23:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(361752, 28351, 8911, '<td valign="top">Cute! I like the focus; the wave being slightly out of focus, but not strongly so, works especially well.</td>', 'Cute! I like the focus; the wave being slightly out of focus, but not strongly so, works especially well.', '2003-07-20 23:25:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(361753, 28591, 8911, '<td valign="top">This was good for a definite giggle - very cute. Nice layout of the entombed peppers, also. I wonder whether softer lighting might have been better - the light on the peppers and ice cubes works well, but the reflections in the water droplets and off the plastic (?) backdrop, I find a bit distracting.</td>', 'This was good for a definite giggle - very cute. Nice layout of the entombed peppers, also. I wonder whether softer lighting might have been better - the light on the peppers and ice cubes works well, but the reflections in the water droplets and off the plastic (?) backdrop, I find a bit distracting.', '2003-07-20 23:26:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(361756, 28506, 8911, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid I don''t get a sense of temperature from this - a definite sense of something night-time possibly involving emergency vehicles or a tow truck, but no sense of temperature. It''s quite probable the elements are there, but this image is very small - at less than 200 pixels on a side, it is hard to see any detail. Up to 640 pixels are allowed on a side - there''s allowance for a lot more detail than we can see in an image that''s this small physically.<br/> <br/>File size can be up to 150 k - it looks like yours is only 6k - so even for the physical size of the image, it''s probably not giving us very much detail.<br/> <br/>If you need help with sizing - check out the forums (see the community link in the menu). I had some trouble with file size (rather than display size) early on and got some great advice from one of the threads there as well as comments on my photos.</td>', 'I''m afraid I don''t get a sense of temperature from this - a definite sense of something night-time possibly involving emergency vehicles or a tow truck, but no sense of temperature. It''s quite probable the elements are there, but this image is very small - at less than 200 pixels on a side, it is hard to see any detail. Up to 640 pixels are allowed on a side - there''s allowance for a lot more detail than we can see in an image that''s this small physically. File size can be up to 150 k - it looks like yours is only 6k - so even for the physical size of the image, it''s probably not giving us very much detail. If you need help with sizing - check out the forums (see the community link in the menu). I had some trouble with file size (rather than display size) early on and got some great advice from one of the threads there as well as comments on my photos.', '2003-07-20 23:31:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(361763, 28385, 255, '<td valign="top">nice--i dig this. nice lighting-- i like the variation of colors. i like the dof too. the only nit pic i have is the border--it detracts from the impact of the lighting, i think.</td>', 'nice--i dig this. nice lighting-- i like the variation of colors. i like the dof too. the only nit pic i have is the border--it detracts from the impact of the lighting, i think.', '2003-07-20 23:54:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(361765, 28653, 2130, '<td valign="top">this one is fun, a 9 from me</td>', 'this one is fun, a 9 from me', '2003-07-20 23:55:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(361766, 28707, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like this - colors, composition - it matches the title nicely (although, objectively, I''m not sure heat is required for a shot like this, it still _feels_ hot to look at it). I like the buildings, the way they break the line of the horizon. The painterly feel of the sky is lovely. This is not only a good temperature photo, but an excellent photo in general.</td>', 'I like this - colors, composition - it matches the title nicely (although, objectively, I''m not sure heat is required for a shot like this, it still _feels_ hot to look at it). I like the buildings, the way they break the line of the horizon. The painterly feel of the sky is lovely. This is not only a good temperature photo, but an excellent photo in general.', '2003-07-20 23:55:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(361768, 28548, 8911, '<td valign="top">Nice, nice, nice. This wouldn''t be half so powerful witou the sunset for a backdrop, tracing lips and reflecting in the ice. Lovely colors and nice timing, to catch the drop as it falls!</td>', 'Nice, nice, nice. This wouldn''t be half so powerful witou the sunset for a backdrop, tracing lips and reflecting in the ice. Lovely colors and nice timing, to catch the drop as it falls!', '2003-07-21 00:03:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(361772, 28563, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a nice, contented picture - I like the "vintage" feel it has. Not quite sure why it works for me - I can look at it logically, technically, and not see anything to really say, anything that really stands out to me (at my level of knowledge) - and yet it all comes together very nicely.</td>', 'This is a nice, contented picture - I like the "vintage" feel it has. Not quite sure why it works for me - I can look at it logically, technically, and not see anything to really say, anything that really stands out to me (at my level of knowledge) - and yet it all comes together very nicely.', '2003-07-21 00:10:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(361773, 28589, 8911, '<td valign="top">Good for a definite giggle, though the rounding on one side looks more pan-based than street-based. I''ve definitely met days that felt like this looks, though!</td>', 'Good for a definite giggle, though the rounding on one side looks more pan-based than street-based. I''ve definitely met days that felt like this looks, though!', '2003-07-21 00:11:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(361775, 28180, 8911, '<td valign="top">Very cool (sorry, I had to pun). I like the effect of the fingers through the ice, the difference between the ice and the snow in the background. Please say you were careful to warm fingers up after each take on this one though! Makes mine ache just to think about it....</td>', 'Very cool (sorry, I had to pun). I like the effect of the fingers through the ice, the difference between the ice and the snow in the background. Please say you were careful to warm fingers up after each take on this one though! Makes mine ache just to think about it....', '2003-07-21 00:12:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(361778, 28449, 8911, '<td valign="top">I love the cool colors/feeling of the background, especially contrasted with the warmer colors of the foreground. I could wish the focus felt more "crisp" on the body as well as the face, though.</td>', 'I love the cool colors/feeling of the background, especially contrasted with the warmer colors of the foreground. I could wish the focus felt more "crisp" on the body as well as the face, though.', '2003-07-21 00:13:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(361779, 28607, 5705, '<td valign="top">Nice Flame Shot</td>', 'Nice Flame Shot', '2003-07-21 00:14:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(361783, 28653, 8911, '<td valign="top">*g* Very cute. Like the very low perspective on this one, the grit in the egg. Looks like it could have been cooked there, though the torn-up bit to the right side suggests it was moved - wonder if a slightly different angle could have hidden that without introducing other unwanted elements....</td>', '*g* Very cute. Like the very low perspective on this one, the grit in the egg. Looks like it could have been cooked there, though the torn-up bit to the right side suggests it was moved - wonder if a slightly different angle could have hidden that without introducing other unwanted elements....', '2003-07-21 00:17:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(361784, 28763, 8911, '<td valign="top">Very attractive - nice, cool colors, very crisp in the shadows. A bit washed-out as far as detail in the brightest areas, which is a bit of a pity, but a worthwhile tradeoff to get those hints of reflections even in the deep shadow.</td>', 'Very attractive - nice, cool colors, very crisp in the shadows. A bit washed-out as far as detail in the brightest areas, which is a bit of a pity, but a worthwhile tradeoff to get those hints of reflections even in the deep shadow.', '2003-07-21 00:18:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(361785, 28529, 5705, '<td valign="top">This is a very original and well shot photograph-- in my top 3<br/>10!!</td>', 'This is a very original and well shot photograph-- in my top 310!!', '2003-07-21 00:19:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(361788, 28544, 8911, '<td valign="top">Brrr. A very artistic feel to this one, too, as though I am looking at some sort of bizarre sculpture. I wonder what this would look like with a more painterly/blurred effect, or in a more sharply vertical format to resemble a wall-hanging? I like it as it is, but it reminds me somewhat of some Japanese art - I''m not sure why - which is why the thoughts on format.</td>', 'Brrr. A very artistic feel to this one, too, as though I am looking at some sort of bizarre sculpture. I wonder what this would look like with a more painterly/blurred effect, or in a more sharply vertical format to resemble a wall-hanging? I like it as it is, but it reminds me somewhat of some Japanese art - I''m not sure why - which is why the thoughts on format.', '2003-07-21 00:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(361789, 28738, 5705, '<td valign="top">This is a spectacular image!<br/> <br/>The shutter speed is as close to perfect as you can get, it just wondefull.<br/> <br/>9<br/></td>', 'This is a spectacular image! The shutter speed is as close to perfect as you can get, it just wondefull. 9', '2003-07-21 00:20:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(361791, 28529, 8911, '<td valign="top">Dry ice? I wouldn''t expect the mist from regular ice, but it makes a nice effect. The lighting on this is also very attractive.</td>', 'Dry ice? I wouldn''t expect the mist from regular ice, but it makes a nice effect. The lighting on this is also very attractive.', '2003-07-21 00:20:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(361792, 28207, 8911, '<td valign="top">Man, he looks comfortable. What a naturally beautiful location - and a nice crisp photograph of it also. I like the feel of the photograph, though I can''t think of any more detailed comment on it than that.</td>', 'Man, he looks comfortable. What a naturally beautiful location - and a nice crisp photograph of it also. I like the feel of the photograph, though I can''t think of any more detailed comment on it than that.', '2003-07-21 00:22:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(361797, 28555, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like the very vertical format on this one - it doesn''t strongly convey heat to me, though. The sun glare is balanced pleasantly by the greenery at the bottom. I can believe that it''s hot, it just wouldn''t jump out at me as such without the title and the challenge topic.</td>', 'I like the very vertical format on this one - it doesn''t strongly convey heat to me, though. The sun glare is balanced pleasantly by the greenery at the bottom. I can believe that it''s hot, it just wouldn''t jump out at me as such without the title and the challenge topic.', '2003-07-21 00:24:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(361798, 28126, 6870, '<td valign="top">Oh yeah! They are hot! And a  hot photo! N ice candid and super lighting. Great thinking and quick reaction I''m sure! 9</td>', 'Oh yeah! They are hot! And a  hot photo! N ice candid and super lighting. Great thinking and quick reaction I''m sure! 9', '2003-07-21 00:24:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(361799, 28757, 8911, '<td valign="top">I''m not so sure this looks frigid - it looks more like a defrosting session where it''s warming up and melting. Regardless, it definitely conveys a temperature that''s cool if not downright code. The half-cut-off dial in the lower left is a bit distracting, even as it gives a sense of what the photo''s about, though.</td>', 'I''m not so sure this looks frigid - it looks more like a defrosting session where it''s warming up and melting. Regardless, it definitely conveys a temperature that''s cool if not downright code. The half-cut-off dial in the lower left is a bit distracting, even as it gives a sense of what the photo''s about, though.', '2003-07-21 00:25:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(361800, 28749, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like this - very traditional, and amusing. I''d swear I see fibers from something like cotton, though - not sure if I''m imagining that or not, however.</td>', 'I like this - very traditional, and amusing. I''d swear I see fibers from something like cotton, though - not sure if I''m imagining that or not, however.', '2003-07-21 00:26:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(361801, 28621, 8911, '<td valign="top">I wish I had more a sense of place or object on this. Ice cubes, apparently melting on something - but the ice cubes are cut off and focus is given to what I assume is the meltwater, and just the edge of what it''s sitting on. The reflections are highly blurred. It definitely evokes temperature - but I keep wishing I could see either a bit more or a bit less,. I think it may be partly that the cubes are cut off, and partly that the line of the water''s edge leads my eye up and out of the frame without going near the cubes.</td>', 'I wish I had more a sense of place or object on this. Ice cubes, apparently melting on something - but the ice cubes are cut off and focus is given to what I assume is the meltwater, and just the edge of what it''s sitting on. The reflections are highly blurred. It definitely evokes temperature - but I keep wishing I could see either a bit more or a bit less,. I think it may be partly that the cubes are cut off, and partly that the line of the water''s edge leads my eye up and out of the frame without going near the cubes.', '2003-07-21 00:28:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(361802, 28466, 8911, '<td valign="top">The focus is cooking on gas - but rather than either the food or the burner being the focus, it looks like the spatula and far side of the pan are. The light glare off the near side of the pan is also a bit distracting. This is a nice composition - I''d have liked to see it with a different focus. The way the steam is captured is very nice.</td>', 'The focus is cooking on gas - but rather than either the food or the burner being the focus, it looks like the spatula and far side of the pan are. The light glare off the near side of the pan is also a bit distracting. This is a nice composition - I''d have liked to see it with a different focus. The way the steam is captured is very nice.', '2003-07-21 00:30:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(361805, 28767, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a nice idea - and the reflections would be cool - but I can''t really tell these are frozen. The image seems to have a very heavy grain/speckling going on, so that the bottles and their reflections are marked by spots of color that don''t make sense to me. I''m not sure if there was something colored in the bottles, or if this was a low-light or low-resolution photo that just didn''t have enough information to make a picture this size. I''d like to see what it would look like without that.</td>', 'This is a nice idea - and the reflections would be cool - but I can''t really tell these are frozen. The image seems to have a very heavy grain/speckling going on, so that the bottles and their reflections are marked by spots of color that don''t make sense to me. I''m not sure if there was something colored in the bottles, or if this was a low-light or low-resolution photo that just didn''t have enough information to make a picture this size. I''d like to see what it would look like without that.', '2003-07-21 00:32:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(361807, 28433, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is interesting, but no strong sense of temperature here - are these candles? I''m not sure. The glares of light would seem to perhaps come from flames, but they''re bright enough to have washed out the adjacent areas if so. I can''t make out the forms clearly.<br/> <br/>Most of all, I wish this had been larger - it would be nice to see more of the details.</td>', 'This is interesting, but no strong sense of temperature here - are these candles? I''m not sure. The glares of light would seem to perhaps come from flames, but they''re bright enough to have washed out the adjacent areas if so. I can''t make out the forms clearly. Most of all, I wish this had been larger - it would be nice to see more of the details.', '2003-07-21 00:33:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(361809, 28591, 9232, '<td valign="top">Good idea.  Very creative.<br/> <br/>The lighting is a little hot on some of the ice cubes but the matte finish to the plastic bag (my assumption) under the cubes in the shot helps to dull down the light.  This shows some forethought.  I like the way the hot subjects tend to protrude from the cold storage.</td>', 'Good idea.  Very creative. The lighting is a little hot on some of the ice cubes but the matte finish to the plastic bag (my assumption) under the cubes in the shot helps to dull down the light.  This shows some forethought.  I like the way the hot subjects tend to protrude from the cold storage.', '2003-07-21 00:43:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(361812, 28738, 9232, '<td valign="top">This shot has a quality that invites many viewers in.  Whether you went to a city park, an amusement park or your grandmother''s yard where you pointed the water hose straight up in the air and just stood and felt the droplets falling on your head, most people have had some experience where they enjoyed the cool water keeping them from overheating in the summer.</td>', 'This shot has a quality that invites many viewers in.  Whether you went to a city park, an amusement park or your grandmother''s yard where you pointed the water hose straight up in the air and just stood and felt the droplets falling on your head, most people have had some experience where they enjoyed the cool water keeping them from overheating in the summer.', '2003-07-21 00:45:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(361815, 28586, 9232, '<td valign="top">This picture has an organic, alive feeling that makes me almost tend to smell the gasoline, sweat and cut grass.  The angles of the picture help to make it seem more realistic in my opinion but the image wouldn''t have suffered from slightly tilting it closer to upright.  The sunlight off the chain link feence (seen between the mower''s handle and the engine) is too hot and creates a white area with no definition.  This photo probably could have benefitted if the artist moved about 2 steps to the left before taking this picture.</td>', 'This picture has an organic, alive feeling that makes me almost tend to smell the gasoline, sweat and cut grass.  The angles of the picture help to make it seem more realistic in my opinion but the image wouldn''t have suffered from slightly tilting it closer to upright.  The sunlight off the chain link feence (seen between the mower''s handle and the engine) is too hot and creates a white area with no definition.  This photo probably could have benefitted if the artist moved about 2 steps to the left before taking this picture.', '2003-07-21 00:48:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(361816, 28529, 7339, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot. Not only does it scream cold to me, I love the subject as well. Great focus and comp, lighting is really sweet too. And I love the wisps of cold air breezin by. Excellent shot and highest rated with a 9.</td>', 'I really like this shot. Not only does it scream cold to me, I love the subject as well. Great focus and comp, lighting is really sweet too. And I love the wisps of cold air breezin by. Excellent shot and highest rated with a 9.', '2003-07-21 00:49:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(361818, 28256, 8953, '<td valign="top">This would have worked in the new challenge "Contrast" no question some of that grass got a little warm.</td>', 'This would have worked in the new challenge "Contrast" no question some of that grass got a little warm.', '2003-07-21 00:52:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(361821, 28092, 8953, '<td valign="top">what a disaster! but the image is first rate the flame, ash, smoke and ruins come to gether so well. I cant make my mind up about the tree...I think it adds to the perspective. good job 8</td>', 'what a disaster! but the image is first rate the flame, ash, smoke and ruins come to gether so well. I cant make my mind up about the tree...I think it adds to the perspective. good job 8', '2003-07-21 00:54:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(361822, 28400, 7339, '<td valign="top">Hot stuff here!  I am partial to flame myself and really appreciate this photo. Great sharpness on the bottle along with the slight tilt too it. The flame background really works well and has no distracting spots in my opinion. I know from personal experience with this type of shot its not to easy to get the flame to come out as smooth and balanced as you did. Great Job -- 8</td>', 'Hot stuff here!  I am partial to flame myself and really appreciate this photo. Great sharpness on the bottle along with the slight tilt too it. The flame background really works well and has no distracting spots in my opinion. I know from personal experience with this type of shot its not to easy to get the flame to come out as smooth and balanced as you did. Great Job -- 8', '2003-07-21 00:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(361824, 28529, 6900, '<td valign="top">Best of the week.  Top 2 for sure. 10</td>', 'Best of the week.  Top 2 for sure. 10', '2003-07-21 00:54:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(361825, 28400, 6900, '<td valign="top">Blue or Red - nothing below that.  This has to ribbon.  10 here, excellent work.  It''s perfect.</td>', 'Blue or Red - nothing below that.  This has to ribbon.  10 here, excellent work.  It''s perfect.', '2003-07-21 00:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(361830, 28615, 6900, '<td valign="top">How fun!  These guys look happy!  :)  And like they''re about to get mom or dad wet.  Good luck!  (If I had to change anything, I''d move right a bit and shoot left so the swingset-thing is out of the shot.  I love their expressions - did you have it on burst and pick the best?)</td>', 'How fun!  These guys look happy!  :)  And like they''re about to get mom or dad wet.  Good luck!  (If I had to change anything, I''d move right a bit and shoot left so the swingset-thing is out of the shot.  I love their expressions - did you have it on burst and pick the best?)', '2003-07-21 00:56:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(361833, 28548, 7339, '<td valign="top">Very nice. Excellent composer and use of available light. This looks like a tough shot and I am impressed with the droplet capture with out the look of flash on her face and beautiful lips. Great job -- 8</td>', 'Very nice. Excellent composer and use of available light. This looks like a tough shot and I am impressed with the droplet capture with out the look of flash on her face and beautiful lips. Great job -- 8', '2003-07-21 00:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(361834, 28073, 6900, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of carolee''s chess shot.  I like this a lot - would be even better with less ice so that the blue came thru the glass a bit.  Like the water drops and the reflections are minimized.  Excellent work. 9</td>', 'Reminds me of carolee''s chess shot.  I like this a lot - would be even better with less ice so that the blue came thru the glass a bit.  Like the water drops and the reflections are minimized.  Excellent work. 9', '2003-07-21 00:57:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(361835, 28548, 6900, '<td valign="top">Not fond of the grain.  Excellent shot overall tho.</td>', 'Not fond of the grain.  Excellent shot overall tho.', '2003-07-21 00:57:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(361836, 27918, 7969, '<td valign="top">I commented on your shot earlier but i see it didnt go through-- i love the expression in his eyes,  he looks like he is having a sensual experience, I also like you can see his partly blue tongue.  Thanks for sharing this shot it really made me smile.  nice work  :  )</td>', 'I commented on your shot earlier but i see it didnt go through-- i love the expression in his eyes,  he looks like he is having a sensual experience, I also like you can see his partly blue tongue.  Thanks for sharing this shot it really made me smile.  nice work  :  )', '2003-07-21 00:58:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(361837, 28092, 6900, '<td valign="top">One of the most dramatic images in all of dpc.  I hope this is top 3.  (probably 3rd if it is).  I know things like this are hard to "think" about shooting, but did you use burst and pick out the best?  Could you have moved so that branch wasn''t in the way?  Again - nitpicking.  10</td>', 'One of the most dramatic images in all of dpc.  I hope this is top 3.  (probably 3rd if it is).  I know things like this are hard to "think" about shooting, but did you use burst and pick out the best?  Could you have moved so that branch wasn''t in the way?  Again - nitpicking.  10', '2003-07-21 00:58:59.000000', NULL, 1),
