(362263, 28529, 6870, '<td valign="top">As some have guessed, this is dry ice. At least partially. I found out a few years ago while entering some home made ice cream into a cooking contest that normal water ice on top of dry ice causes a slight steamy effect. I added just a touch of water to this. Thanks for the votes, all!</td>', 'As some have guessed, this is dry ice. At least partially. I found out a few years ago while entering some home made ice cream into a cooking contest that normal water ice on top of dry ice causes a slight steamy effect. I added just a touch of water to this. Thanks for the votes, all!', '2003-07-21 11:05:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(362276, 28385, 5982, '<td valign="top">Back to you dsidwell!!!  thanks!</td>', 'Back to you dsidwell!!!  thanks!', '2003-07-21 11:15:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(362295, 28400, 7291, '<td valign="top">I knew this would get a ribbon, but I had hoped for a Blue Ribbon for this picture.  Great Job, Great Pic!</td>', 'I knew this would get a ribbon, but I had hoped for a Blue Ribbon for this picture.  Great Job, Great Pic!', '2003-07-21 11:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(362313, 28749, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/> <br/>Very orginal in this challenge.  This has a wonderful feeling of the cold artic blast that comes with a York Peppermint Pattie, according to the commerical. =o)<br/> <br/>Seriously your dof used here is very shallow and works very well for this photo.  Your lighting is really good, you have very limited shadowing. There is a wonderful texture here were you can see the fibers and also the grains of sugar.<br/> <br/>I''m guessing you broke off the missing piece of the peppermint pattie cause it is so smooth and might have made more of a statement had it been bitten off with teethmarks visable rather than broken off.<br/> <br/>It really is a cool photo and looks really good.  Well done!<br/> <br/>Anna<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club  Very orginal in this challenge.  This has a wonderful feeling of the cold artic blast that comes with a York Peppermint Pattie, according to the commerical. =o) Seriously your dof used here is very shallow and works very well for this photo.  Your lighting is really good, you have very limited shadowing. There is a wonderful texture here were you can see the fibers and also the grains of sugar. I''m guessing you broke off the missing piece of the peppermint pattie cause it is so smooth and might have made more of a statement had it been bitten off with teethmarks visable rather than broken off. It really is a cool photo and looks really good.  Well done! Anna ', '2003-07-21 11:43:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(362351, 28529, 806, '<td valign="top">Congrats on third place! Bravo!</td>', 'Congrats on third place! Bravo!', '2003-07-21 12:13:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(362354, 28400, 806, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a great job! well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'Congrats on a great job! well deserved ribbon!', '2003-07-21 12:14:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(362425, 28558, 9661, '<td valign="top">Many of you commented on the pixellation of the printed image.. This was in fact my test sequence and I printed them in draft.. The only problem was none of the other sequences burned so well without curling, falling off the peg.. you name it.. Valuable lesson for me though.. Thanks for all your comments..</td>', 'Many of you commented on the pixellation of the printed image.. This was in fact my test sequence and I printed them in draft.. The only problem was none of the other sequences burned so well without curling, falling off the peg.. you name it.. Valuable lesson for me though.. Thanks for all your comments..', '2003-07-21 13:12:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(362429, 28092, 10145, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot~!  Limb adds contrast between living and dead...</td>', 'Very cool shot~!  Limb adds contrast between living and dead...', '2003-07-21 13:19:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(362458, 28498, 7339, '<td valign="top">&lt;--Critique Club --&gt;<br/> <br/>Funny, my first Critique as a CC member is a nipple; my wife would say "it figures".<br/> <br/>First off, I think this is a good idea for temperature and does bring cold to my mind (among other things). <br/> <br/>So how would I improve on this image? <br/> <br/>First I would have shown more of the breast, perhaps backing out far enough to see both sides, while also showing the finger tips holding the ice cube, although adding that may have been interesting but at the same time might have taken away from the overall focus of the image. <br/> <br/>As far as the nipple itself, I would have moved slightly down a bit probably about 3 inches or so to show an almost side view of it because the area above and to the left is drawing my eye there, taking the attention away from the droplet coming from the ice cube. Also the droplet on the left of the breast is a bit (not too much, just a little) distracting.  <br/> <br/>Overall its really good idea for temperature, nice job.<br/></td>', '<--Critique Club --> Funny, my first Critique as a CC member is a nipple; my wife would say "it figures". First off, I think this is a good idea for temperature and does bring cold to my mind (among other things).  So how would I improve on this image?  First I would have shown more of the breast, perhaps backing out far enough to see both sides, while also showing the finger tips holding the ice cube, although adding that may have been interesting but at the same time might have taken away from the overall focus of the image.  As far as the nipple itself, I would have moved slightly down a bit probably about 3 inches or so to show an almost side view of it because the area above and to the left is drawing my eye there, taking the attention away from the droplet coming from the ice cube. Also the droplet on the left of the breast is a bit (not too much, just a little) distracting.   Overall its really good idea for temperature, nice job.', '2003-07-21 13:36:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(362478, 28548, 4493, '<td valign="top">Top work, I gave this one a ten and had thought it''d place 1st. Very pro shot!</td>', 'Top work, I gave this one a ten and had thought it''d place 1st. Very pro shot!', '2003-07-21 14:05:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(362480, 28400, 8682, '<td valign="top">Congrats for this ribbon! It´s a really great work. For me, this picture is the best one of this week. One of my favourite.</td>', 'Congrats for this ribbon! It´s a really great work. For me, this picture is the best one of this week. One of my favourite.', '2003-07-21 14:12:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(362515, 28529, 1031, '<td valign="top">For some reason this reminds me more of a zombie movie effect ("Night of the Living Oreos") than cold temerature, although I guess you could say that is spine-chilling. Somewhat similar feel to my photo "Cereal Killers."<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-21 13:49:34.</i></td>', 'For some reason this reminds me more of a zombie movie effect ("Night of the Living Oreos") than cold temerature, although I guess you could say that is spine-chilling. Somewhat similar feel to my photo "Cereal Killers."', '2003-07-21 14:48:29.000000', '2003-07-21 14:49:34.000000', 0),
(362537, 28092, 715, '<td valign="top">Congrats with this amazing photo!</td>', 'Congrats with this amazing photo!', '2003-07-21 15:23:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(362603, 28529, 7033, '<td valign="top">Great shot, David!<br/> <br/>Having played with dry ice while making homemade rootbeer a few times, I can almost feel the cold!  Great capture!  Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?</td>', 'Great shot, David! Having played with dry ice while making homemade rootbeer a few times, I can almost feel the cold!  Great capture!  Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?', '2003-07-21 16:54:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(362644, 28529, 4090, '<td valign="top">Congratulations David ... Yet another great shot .</td>', 'Congratulations David ... Yet another great shot .', '2003-07-21 17:33:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(362722, 27782, 6405, '<td valign="top">Done in Super Macro on my balcony.</td>', 'Done in Super Macro on my balcony.', '2003-07-21 18:55:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(362791, 28400, 5573, '<td valign="top">Thanks very much for the encouragement!! This was a fun shot to do. I set up the bottle in front of my computer screen with a fire background displayed. I tried it with hot sauce in the bottle but it looked too dark. I used aperature priority to get the blur I wanted on the background. Thanks again.<br/>p.s. The voting breakdown chart is interesting. Check it out.</td>', 'Thanks very much for the encouragement!! This was a fun shot to do. I set up the bottle in front of my computer screen with a fire background displayed. I tried it with hot sauce in the bottle but it looked too dark. I used aperature priority to get the blur I wanted on the background. Thanks again.p.s. The voting breakdown chart is interesting. Check it out.', '2003-07-21 20:14:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(362867, 28591, 4967, '<td valign="top">This is cute... very very original idea!  I like it... from the thumbnail I thought there were goldfish in the icecubes!  hehehe... I''m relieved that it''s chillies instead.  Very nicely done. I''m adding it to my faves<br/></td>', 'This is cute... very very original idea!  I like it... from the thumbnail I thought there were goldfish in the icecubes!  hehehe... I''m relieved that it''s chillies instead.  Very nicely done. I''m adding it to my faves', '2003-07-21 21:32:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(362882, 28702, 6900, '<td valign="top">Why?!  lol<br/>Just curious of course...maybe I would "learn" to "see" it.</td>', 'Why?!  lolJust curious of course...maybe I would "learn" to "see" it.', '2003-07-21 21:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(362906, 28702, 472, '<td valign="top">the light mostly. and the colors. but the way the light shines through the red fluid .. :) <br/> <br/></td>', 'the light mostly. and the colors. but the way the light shines through the red fluid .. :)  ', '2003-07-21 22:08:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(363190, 28529, 6870, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pncowley:</b></div><hr/><i>Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good question. When I find that out, I''ll let you know, but it''s probably the same reason I used green kisses and a red apple in another of my shots. Maybe I''m just bizarre!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-22 03:10:14.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by pncowley:Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?  Good question. When I find that out, I''ll let you know, but it''s probably the same reason I used green kisses and a red apple in another of my shots. Maybe I''m just bizarre!', '2003-07-22 04:09:37.000000', '2003-07-22 04:10:14.000000', 0),
