(363855, 28092, 4182, '<td valign="top">i think it is hilarious that there is such a difference in opinion over the tree branch .. i don find it annoying ... but i dont really feel it adds a ''live'' aspect to the image either .. i just think it is there and thats ok.<br/>I guess as thats what most people are commenting on I would on after view say well even though this shot won .. maybe a better version would be more of the tree .. or none of the tree ..  it''s nice to learn from others in such a way sometimes ..</td>', 'i think it is hilarious that there is such a difference in opinion over the tree branch .. i don find it annoying ... but i dont really feel it adds a ''live'' aspect to the image either .. i just think it is there and thats ok.I guess as thats what most people are commenting on I would on after view say well even though this shot won .. maybe a better version would be more of the tree .. or none of the tree ..  it''s nice to learn from others in such a way sometimes ..', '2003-07-22 21:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(363858, 28529, 4182, '<td valign="top">oreos .. on ice ... nice .. i like the dreamy effect cool<br/> <br/>i was gonna ask why oreos too ... you know what i would like ot see ... is a perfect pint of guiness shot in the same way .. or maybe a can .. <br/> <br/>i odnt know why i want to see that ... i just do ... kinda for the same reason you shot oreos ... you just dont know !</td>', 'oreos .. on ice ... nice .. i like the dreamy effect cool i was gonna ask why oreos too ... you know what i would like ot see ... is a perfect pint of guiness shot in the same way .. or maybe a can ..  i odnt know why i want to see that ... i just do ... kinda for the same reason you shot oreos ... you just dont know !', '2003-07-22 21:13:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(365003, 28400, 8860, '<td valign="top">Have you wondered who the hell voted you 1s? It''s a ''hot'' product on a hot background and the challenge is ''Temperature''! Now by any stretch of the imagination or technical critique this does not deserve a 1 (let alone 2s and 3s). Who are these people?<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon<br/> <br/>. : <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/portfolio.php?USER_ID=8860.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gallery</a> : : <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=8860.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Profile</a> : .</td>', 'Have you wondered who the hell voted you 1s? It''s a ''hot'' product on a hot background and the challenge is ''Temperature''! Now by any stretch of the imagination or technical critique this does not deserve a 1 (let alone 2s and 3s). Who are these people? CheersJon . : Gallery : : Profile : .', '2003-07-23 14:21:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(365274, 28755, 7504, '<td valign="top">Hey Gracious.  This was my favorite shot of the challenge.  Love the composition, the border, everything.  It''s abstract, and it fits the challenge to a T.  Nice work!</td>', 'Hey Gracious.  This was my favorite shot of the challenge.  Love the composition, the border, everything.  It''s abstract, and it fits the challenge to a T.  Nice work!', '2003-07-23 19:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(365700, 28400, 6349, '<td valign="top">Hey.  Congrats.  I did a hotsauce and fire shot with the exact same title though....still, mine wasn''t nearly as good (but I should have saved such an idea for the temperature challenge huh !?)  I should have done the computer background thing though instead of trying to wave a lighter around in front of the image of the bottle on the screen.  I guess i just did things backwards and paid the price!  lol.  Thanks for the learning experience of compare/contrast.</td>', 'Hey.  Congrats.  I did a hotsauce and fire shot with the exact same title though....still, mine wasn''t nearly as good (but I should have saved such an idea for the temperature challenge huh !?)  I should have done the computer background thing though instead of trying to wave a lighter around in front of the image of the bottle on the screen.  I guess i just did things backwards and paid the price!  lol.  Thanks for the learning experience of compare/contrast.', '2003-07-24 02:54:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(366621, 28529, 10145, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorite shots on dpc.  Love the dreamy effect...it speaks volumes!</td>', 'This is one of my favorite shots on dpc.  Love the dreamy effect...it speaks volumes!', '2003-07-25 10:24:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(366628, 28400, 10145, '<td valign="top">Great photo! Love the fire effect...this is more effective without the hotsauce in the bottle...keep em coming!</td>', 'Great photo! Love the fire effect...this is more effective without the hotsauce in the bottle...keep em coming!', '2003-07-25 10:52:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(366630, 28092, 10145, '<td valign="top">As an afterthought....the tree branches seem to represent a small portion of life watching, waiting helplessly while it observes the tradgedy at hand. It is a necessary element to this photo. You can almost feel the intense heat from the flames. This is a great picture with a statement. Good work Rick! Well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'As an afterthought....the tree branches seem to represent a small portion of life watching, waiting helplessly while it observes the tradgedy at hand. It is a necessary element to this photo. You can almost feel the intense heat from the flames. This is a great picture with a statement. Good work Rick! Well deserved ribbon!', '2003-07-25 10:57:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(367148, 28529, 10402, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dsidwell:</b></div><hr/><i><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pncowley:</b></div><hr/><i>Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good question. When I find that out, I''ll let you know, but it''s probably the same reason I used green kisses and a red apple in another of my shots. Maybe I''m just bizarre!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ll vouch for bizarre. But I can''t think of anything better to use. The dark Oreos contrast with the light fog and have an interesting texture. Nice choice of color, and the swirling details in the fog were captured perfectly.</td>', 'Originally posted by dsidwell:Originally posted by pncowley:Just one question, though... what made you choose oreos for the balance of the shot?  Good question. When I find that out, I''ll let you know, but it''s probably the same reason I used green kisses and a red apple in another of my shots. Maybe I''m just bizarre!  I''ll vouch for bizarre. But I can''t think of anything better to use. The dark Oreos contrast with the light fog and have an interesting texture. Nice choice of color, and the swirling details in the fog were captured perfectly.', '2003-07-26 00:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(367762, 28598, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Good take on the challenge with Isaac. =o)  Psst Paul make sure you wind the windows down when the ac isn''t working.  LOL joking aside...It is a little dark and also there is a bit of a green cast.  But the focus and sharpness seem just fine.  <br/> <br/>Meets the challenge well.  Isaac looks really hot!  <br/> <br/>Anna</td>', '*Critique Club* Good take on the challenge with Isaac. =o)  Psst Paul make sure you wind the windows down when the ac isn''t working.  LOL joking aside...It is a little dark and also there is a bit of a green cast.  But the focus and sharpness seem just fine.   Meets the challenge well.  Isaac looks really hot!   Anna', '2003-07-27 14:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(367895, 28400, 8283, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Kind of reminds me of New Orleans cuisine.</td>', 'Great shot! Kind of reminds me of New Orleans cuisine.', '2003-07-27 18:37:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(368028, 28678, 7339, '<td valign="top">&lt;-- Critique Club --&gt;<br/> <br/>Heres the Critique you requested.<br/> <br/>The idea of this photo is good but its difficult to figure out what your seeing. The point where the 2 ice cubes are "kissing" is being over shadowed by the blackness of the background and what seems to be another cube to the left. <br/> <br/>Perhaps if you pulled back a little farther to show more of the top ice cube that may help. Also if you brightened up the photo all together that might help too.<br/> <br/>Good luck on future challenges.<br/> <br/>Diversq<br/></td>', '<-- Critique Club --> Heres the Critique you requested. The idea of this photo is good but its difficult to figure out what your seeing. The point where the 2 ice cubes are "kissing" is being over shadowed by the blackness of the background and what seems to be another cube to the left.  Perhaps if you pulled back a little farther to show more of the top ice cube that may help. Also if you brightened up the photo all together that might help too. Good luck on future challenges. Diversq', '2003-07-27 23:48:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(368032, 28712, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE <br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>I really like the deep rich colors on this, and I think the warmth that the picture has really adds to the melting ice effect.  You have done well capturing what had to be a fairly difficult shot with good focus and exposure.  I also like how the out of focus reflection gives it a suspended look.  <br/> <br/>As I mentioned during the challenge, the framing bothers me a touch.  I can see why it is composed as it is (to include the entire reflection), but it still seems a bit tight for me at the top.  Perhaps just a bit more room up there would give it a more open feeling.  Or, if you could have enough space up there to place the flower/ice on the lower horizontal third, it would have a nice balanced feeling, too, I think.  Of course, I understand that by doing that, you may lose some wonderful detail.<br/> <br/>again, a very nice shot that leaves the viewer with just enough questions to make the shot interesting, but not so many as to frustrate him/her.  <br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE by karmat I really like the deep rich colors on this, and I think the warmth that the picture has really adds to the melting ice effect.  You have done well capturing what had to be a fairly difficult shot with good focus and exposure.  I also like how the out of focus reflection gives it a suspended look.   As I mentioned during the challenge, the framing bothers me a touch.  I can see why it is composed as it is (to include the entire reflection), but it still seems a bit tight for me at the top.  Perhaps just a bit more room up there would give it a more open feeling.  Or, if you could have enough space up there to place the flower/ice on the lower horizontal third, it would have a nice balanced feeling, too, I think.  Of course, I understand that by doing that, you may lose some wonderful detail. again, a very nice shot that leaves the viewer with just enough questions to make the shot interesting, but not so many as to frustrate him/her.   Best to you in future challenges. karmat', '2003-07-28 00:11:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(369662, 28466, 5391, '<td valign="top">Huh.  I just saw your comment in the forums and took a look at this.  I gave it a 9.  I thought it was fabulous...  I can''t believe so many people saw this as out of focus.  To me, the softness suggested motion, suggesting stir-frying, suggesting heat.  Really surprised this didn''t do better.</td>', 'Huh.  I just saw your comment in the forums and took a look at this.  I gave it a 9.  I thought it was fabulous...  I can''t believe so many people saw this as out of focus.  To me, the softness suggested motion, suggesting stir-frying, suggesting heat.  Really surprised this didn''t do better.', '2003-07-29 15:27:03.000000', NULL, 0),
